# OPTIONAL — the whole dev stack runs fully stubbed (stub payment dispatcher,
# stub face verifier) with NO infra/.dev.vars file at all. You only need this
# file to opt a worker into a real vendor.
#
# To opt in: copy this file to infra/.dev.vars (same folder — wrangler reads
# .dev.vars next to the --config file, verified: `npx wrangler dev --config
# infra/wrangler.payments.toml` run from the repo root loads
# infra/.dev.vars). infra/.dev.vars is gitignored; NEVER commit real keys.
#
# Every vendor selector and credential line below is commented out ON PURPOSE:
# an uncommented PLACEHOLDER looks like a configured key to the fail-loud
# config guards, so the stack would make live vendor calls with bogus
# credentials instead of refusing to start.
# - Flutterwave block: uncomment ONLY with a real FLWSECK_TEST key from your
#   own dashboard.
# - Smile ID block: uncomment ONLY with real sandbox keys from your own
#   Smile ID dashboard.
#
# These values are read by ALL workers you start with a config in infra/ —
# keys a worker doesn't use are simply ignored.

# ── Payments worker: Flutterwave dispatcher (ADR-0009/0023) ─────────────────
# Uncomment to switch the dispatcher from the dev stub to real test-mode
# transfers — only together with a REAL test key below, never the placeholder:
# PAYMENT_DISPATCHER=flutterwave

# Your Flutterwave TEST secret key (dashboard → Settings → API keys). Test
# keys (FLWSECK_TEST-…) hit the same production host — there is no separate
# sandbox base URL. Uncomment and replace the placeholder:
# FLUTTERWAVE_SECRET_KEY=FLWSECK_TEST-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx-X

# Webhook secret hash: any random string YOU invent (e.g. `openssl rand -hex
# 32`), pasted identically into dashboard → Settings → Webhooks → Secret hash.
# Flutterwave echoes it back in the `verif-hash` header; the worker rejects
# mismatches with 401. Leave unset (commented out) to disable
# /webhooks/transfers (503).
# FLUTTERWAVE_WEBHOOK_SECRET_HASH=

# Optional overrides (defaults shown):
# FLUTTERWAVE_BASE_URL=https://api.flutterwave.com
# FLUTTERWAVE_CALLBACK_URL=

# Test-mode transfer accelerator (LOCAL DEV ONLY — NEVER in production):
# truthy appends the provider's magic `_PMCKDU_1` suffix to every outgoing
# transfer reference (the short provider alias from ADR-0024's amendment) so
# mock transfers settle SUCCESSFUL in ~1 min instead of sitting PENDING ~10 min
# (provider-documented). Webhook/lookup references are stripped back to the
# bare provider alias before row matching, so this is invisible upstream. The
# failure variant `_PMCK_ST_FDU_1` exists for failure drills but is NOT wired —
# append it to a reference manually when drilling.
# FLUTTERWAVE_TEST_MODE=1

# Dev payout recipients (JSON, keyed by partyId). Without it, the demo
# seed's seller stores (the settlement leg's party id is the store display
# name at this stage — e.g. "Amina's Fresh Store"), runner:internal, and
# platform fall back to Flutterwave's documented TEST bank accounts
# (Access Bank 044 / 0690000031-33 — test keys only, no real money moves).
# The fallback is disabled for live keys; explicit entries still apply.
# Example shape (seller key must match the store display name exactly):
# DEV_PAYOUT_RECIPIENTS={"<store display name>":{"bank":"044","account":"0690000031","name":"Test Seller"},"runner:internal":{"bank":"044","account":"0690000032"},"platform":{"bank":"044","account":"0690000033"}}

# Local Postgres (dev) — the payments/archive/identity workers read this:
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:54322/market_runs

# ── Identity worker: hybrid Smile ID Biometric KYC (ADR-0028) ───────────────
# Enrollment becomes an async vendor job; ordinary login/recovery remains
# private local liveness + 1:1. Requires REAL sandbox keys, the private Node
# biometrics service/model, and the IDENTITY_CAPTURES R2 binding from
# infra/wrangler.identity.toml. No native Smile ID mobile package is used.
# FACE_VERIFIER=hybrid
# BIOMETRICS_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8792
# BIOMETRICS_SERVICE_TOKEN=replace-with-a-long-random-private-token

# Smile ID SANDBOX keys (Dashboard → Developer Settings; sandbox and
# production keys are NOT interchangeable). Uncomment and replace the
# placeholders:
# SMILEID_PARTNER_ID=0000
# SMILEID_API_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Environment selector (default shown; sandbox hits testapi.smileidentity.com):
# SMILEID_ENV=sandbox

# Callback URL for job results (optional — when unset, Smile ID uses the
# partner default configured in Dashboard → Developer → Security Settings →
# Callback URLs). Point it at https://<your-host>/callbacks/smileid; webhooks
# are signed (Response-Signature header) and verified with the api key.
# SMILEID_CALLBACK_URL=

# HTTPS URL of the privacy notice shown at capture time — forwarded in the
# vendor consent record (NDPA 2023: biometrics are sensitive personal data).
# SMILEID_PRIVACY_NOTICE_URL=
